intp (0.9.0~rc1-1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Stage 2 complete: the working profiler replaces the scaffold stubs.
    Engines ported-and-frozen from intp-comparison @ 2e87b30fc762
    (see SYNC.md): the v2.1 stable-ABI backend set (procfs/sysfs/
    perf_event_open/resctrl, per-metric fallback chains, graceful
    degradation — unavailable is never silent zero) plus the v3.3
    eBPF/CO-RE engine as higher-priority backends (in-kernel counter
    aggregation, per-cgroup attribution, clean fall-through on
    verifier rejection).
  * Output: jsonl (primary, self-describing), tsv-legacy-v1
    (bit-compatible with the IADA/intp-comparison consumers),
    prometheus text format. --print-schema reports per-metric backend,
    semantic model (ADR-0010), scope, stability, and per-candidate
    rejection reasons.
  * CLI: targeting (-p/-c/--pids/--comm/--target-container), backend
    control (--force-backend/--disable-backend/--disable-metric/
    --list-backends), hardware normalizer overrides; experimental
    surfaces (--target-vm, --portable-metrics) fenced behind
    --experimental per ADR-0008.
  * resctrl RMID hygiene: stale mon_group reaping and a 75% RMID
    budget preflight with fall-through to perf backends.
  * Packaging: bpftool added to Build-Depends (BPF skeleton
    generation); checked-in vmlinux.h fallback keeps chroot/PPA
    builds working without /sys/kernel/btf. Example systemd unit
    ships as documentation only (packaging/systemd/; not installed —
    deferred to 1.0 with a hardening review).
  * Deferred: OTLP sink (post-0.9); dlopen plugin loader (the
    portable-metrics provider is statically linked in this line, so
    no intp-plugin-portable package yet); --serve live values pending
    a libmicrohttpd environment.
  * RELEASE GATE: this is a release candidate. The v0.9.0 tag is
    stamped only after the RDT-testbed validation gate passes
    (tests/regression/run-remote-gate.sh steps 1-6).

 -- André Sacilotto Santos <sacilotto.andre@gmail.com>  Wed, 10 Jun 2026 17:00:00 -0300

intp (0.2.0~placeholder-1) noble; urgency=low

  * Add intp_probe_ebpf() public API + `intp --probe` CLI command:
    asks libbpf whether the kernel accepts a kprobe-type BPF program
    and reports OK / kernel-too-old / not-permitted / unsupported.
    Loads no persistent program; safe for unprivileged callers.
    Pulls libbpf into libintp1's runtime Depends (auto-resolved by
    dh_shlibdeps).
  * Add intp_serve_prometheus() public API + `intp --serve` CLI mode:
    libmicrohttpd-based HTTP server that exposes /metrics in the
    canonical Prometheus text format. The seven core metrics are
    exposed with placeholder zero values and status="placeholder";
    intp_metrics_implemented advertises 0 to make the half-built
    state legible to scrapers. Stage 2 wires the live sampling loop
    into the same endpoint with no API change. Pulls libmicrohttpd
    into libintp1's runtime Depends.
  * Bump upstream version to 0.2.0 to reflect the API additions
    (backward-compatible; SONAME stays libintp.so.0).
  * No metric collection logic added — variant selection between v2
    (pure-C) and v3 (eBPF/CO-RE) remains a Stage 1 decision in
    `intp-comparison`.

 -- André Sacilotto Santos <sacilotto.andre@gmail.com>  Sat, 09 May 2026 17:00:00 +0000

intp (0.1.0~placeholder2-1) noble; urgency=low

  * Re-upload after orig tarball regeneration. The previous
    0.1.0~placeholder-1 orig tarball was created with `git archive`
    run from a subdirectory, which (via cwd-relative pathspec
    matching) captured only packaging/debian/* instead of the full
    upstream tree, so Launchpad's meson configure step found no
    meson.build at the source root.
  * No upstream code changes; this is a pure re-roll of the source
    tarball.

